course: dictionary
lesson: 151
title: Afford: Can You Pay For It?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To afford something means you have enough money, time, or energy for it. It is a word we use a lot with can, could, and be able to. «Food banks give food to families who cannot afford enough.» This means those families do not have enough money to buy the food they need.
explain: Afford does not only mean money. «I can't afford to miss the bus» means you do not have enough time to miss it, because you would be late. «We can't afford to make mistakes» means a mistake would have bad results. So always ask: what would be lost if I did this?
explain: In maths, you compare what you have with the price. If your money is more than or equal to the price, you can afford it. «Pocket money is kept somewhere safe, so you always know what you can afford.» Keep track of your money, then you know what you can buy.
explain: Afford can also mean to give or provide. «The hill affords a fine view» means the hill gives you a good view. This is a formal use, so you will often see it in books and news reports.
fact: To afford something means to have enough money, time, or energy for it.
fact: Afford is usually used with can, could, or be able to, as in «We can't afford a new car».
fact: Affordable means cheap enough for people to pay for.
fact: «Lending money to friends can cause arguments, so many grown-ups only lend what they could afford to lose.»
fact: When the hill «affords a fine view», it gives or provides a fine view. This is a formal meaning.
exercise: «Food banks give food to families who cannot afford enough.» What does afford mean here? | To give away for free | To cook with | *To have enough money to pay for something | To carry home
exercise: «Pocket money is kept somewhere safe, so you always know what you can afford.» What does afford mean? | *To have enough money to pay for it | To lose on purpose | To count every day | To give to a friend
exercise: «I can't afford to miss the bus.» What does afford mean here? | *To have enough time for something | To buy a ticket | To ride a bike | To run very fast
test: «The hill affords a fine view.» What does afford mean in this sentence? | To buy | To climb | To hide | *To give or provide
test: A shop sign says «Affordable prices». What does affordable mean? | Lost forever | Broken | *Cheap enough for people to pay for | Very expensive
exam: «We can't afford to make mistakes.» Which meaning of afford is used here? | *To be able to do something without bad results | To count money carefully | To give or provide | To buy something new
